# S(H)ARP — machine-specific configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit for this machine:   cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored; this file is committed and must never contain a real secret.
#
# Scope: machine identity only — where the data lives and what hardware is here.
# Pipeline behaviour (thresholds, model choice, batch sizes) belongs in the config
# dataclasses in `src/sharp/config.py` or on the CLI, so a run stays reproducible
# from its command line. Every key below is optional; unset falls back to the
# in-repo default shown in the comment.
#
# Real environment variables win over this file, so a one-off override works:
#   SHARP_DEVICE=cpu pixi run python -m sharp.extract_embeddings ...


# ── Data roots ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The usual laptop-vs-server difference. Set SHARP_DATA_ROOT alone and the four
# subdirectories follow it; override an individual one only if it lives elsewhere
# (e.g. raw data on a big shared scratch disk, outputs on local NVMe).
#
# Default: <project root>/data
#SHARP_DATA_ROOT=/scratch/$USER/sharp-data

# Defaults: ${SHARP_DATA_ROOT}/{raw,interim,processed,mock}
# `${VAR}` is expanded, so these can be written in terms of the root above.
#SHARP_RAW_DIR=${SHARP_DATA_ROOT}/raw
#SHARP_INTERIM_DIR=${SHARP_DATA_ROOT}/interim
#SHARP_PROCESSED_DIR=${SHARP_DATA_ROOT}/processed
#SHARP_MOCK_DIR=${SHARP_DATA_ROOT}/mock


# ── Hardware ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Device for the embedding step: auto | cpu | cuda | mps
# "auto" prefers CUDA → MPS → CPU. Pin to cpu on a laptop whose GPU can't hold
# the model; leave unset (auto) on the GPU server.
# Default: auto
#SHARP_DEVICE=auto


# ── Credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# None of the current pipeline steps authenticate anywhere: MiBIG and BGC Atlas
# download over plain HTTPS and the default ESM-2 weights are an ungated Hugging
# Face repo. Keys go here only once a step actually needs one — for example an
# NCBI_API_KEY for higher E-utilities rate limits, or HF_TOKEN if a gated model
# is ever used. Keep real values in `.env`, never in this file.
#NCBI_API_KEY=
#HF_TOKEN=
